# ==========================================================================
#  O42  owl:Class, owl:Ontology, and the rule that everything is declared
# ==========================================================================
#
#  DECIDES
#    The vocabulary becomes an OWL 2 DL ontology: an owl:Ontology node,
#    every class an owl:Class, every property exactly one of object,
#    datatype or annotation, every borrowed term declared, and the profile
#    checker as referee.
#
#  WHY
#    The step from RDFS to OWL 2 DL is mostly declarations. rdfs:Class
#    becomes owl:Class. rdf:Property becomes one of owl:ObjectProperty,
#    owl:DatatypeProperty or owl:AnnotationProperty, and exactly one,
#    because a DL reasoner needs to know whether a property's values are
#    things, values or commentary before it can reason at all. Every term
#    the file mentions is declared, including the borrowed ones, because
#    the profile is checked over the imports closure and the Trail imports
#    nothing. And an owl:Ontology node says what the document is.
#
#    The reward for the discipline is that a checker can now say whether
#    the file is OWL 2 DL, and this lesson's file is. The SPARQL course's
#    README records what it took to get the shipped vocabulary there, and
#    the rules that bit were the ones RDFS never mentions: everything
#    declared; a property is one kind only; a transitive property is non-
#    simple and may not be functional; and an RDF 1.2 triple term has no
#    OWL type, so the property that points at one is an annotation
#    property. Each is a lesson in this module.
#
#    The set reading from o35 now has teeth: an owl:Class is a set the
#    reasoner will draw conclusions about, and a class that was rdfs:Class
#    in module 06 was a set nobody could contradict. The profiles table in
#    the measured line shows where this small file sits: in DL, and in EL,
#    QL and RL too, because it says so little.
#
#  DIAGRAM
#       RDFS                                OWL 2 DL
#
#       bs:Bookshop a rdfs:Class            bs:Bookshop a owl:Class
#       bs:locatedIn a rdf:Property         bs:locatedIn a owl:ObjectProperty      (values are things)
#       bs:founded a rdf:Property           bs:founded a owl:DatatypeProperty      (values are values)
#       rdfs:comment (used, undeclared)     rdfs:comment is built in; skos:definition a owl:AnnotationProperty
#       (no header)                         <.../schema> a owl:Ontology
#
#       the referee:  robot validate-profile --profile DL      in profile / NOT in profile, with the reason
#
#  WHAT TO TAKE AWAY
#    - OWL 2 DL is RDFS plus declarations, and the declarations are what
#      let a reasoner and a checker work.
#    - A property is object, datatype or annotation. One. Decide by
#      asking whether its values are things, values or commentary.
#    - Declare what you borrow. The profile is checked over what is
#      imported, and nothing is.
#
#  TRY IT
#    Delete the line declaring bs:website and run python
#    scripts/check_lessons.py o42: the file falls out of DL, and the
#    checker says which term did it. Put it back. The editor will not
#    object either way; only the referee does.
#
#  CORNER    referent
#  RUNS IN   the browser; the OWL 2 profile verdicts on the MEASURED line come from ROBOT
#  LOAD IT   https://semantechs.co.uk/turtle-editor-viewer/?dot=https%3A%2F%2Fraw.githubusercontent.com%2Fpwin%2FOntology_Course%2Fmain%2Flessons%2F07-owl%2Fo42-owl-class-owl-ontology-and-the-rule-that-everything-is-declared.ttl
#  SOURCES   OWL 2 Structural Specification 5.8 Entity Declarations and Typing
#            https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-syntax/#Entity_Declarations_and_Typing
#            OWL 2 Structural Specification 5.8.1 Typing Constraints of OWL 2 DL
#            https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-syntax/#Typing_Constraints_of_OWL_2_DL
#  MEASURED  parses, 26 triples; 4 classes, 1 object property, 2 datatype properties, 2 individuals; OWL 2 DL/EL/QL/RL; HermiT: consistent, 1 inferred
# ==========================================================================

@prefix bt:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/> .
@prefix bs:   <https://example.org/bookshop-trail/schema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .

skos:prefLabel      a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:definition     a owl:AnnotationProperty .
skos:editorialNote  a owl:AnnotationProperty .

<https://example.org/bookshop-trail/schema>
    a               owl:Ontology ;
    skos:prefLabel  "The Bookshop Trail schema"@en .

bs:Place       a owl:Class ; skos:prefLabel "Place"@en .
bs:Settlement  a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf bs:Place ; skos:prefLabel "Settlement"@en .
bs:Bookshop    a owl:Class ; skos:prefLabel "Bookshop"@en .

bs:locatedIn   a owl:ObjectProperty ;   rdfs:range bs:Settlement ; skos:prefLabel "located in"@en .
bs:founded     a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:integer ;   skos:prefLabel "founded"@en .
bs:website     a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:anyURI ;    skos:prefLabel "website"@en .
skos:Concept   a owl:Class .

bt:shop-inkwell  a bs:Bookshop ; bs:locatedIn bt:place-wigtown ; bs:founded 1979 .
bt:place-wigtown a bs:Settlement .
